sb.msg.agentVerb:
The judgement part of « sb {0} » belongs to your agent. Type it there:
  Claude Code   /sb:{0}
  Codex         $sb {0}
  Pilot         sb {0}   (as a message, if the verb says Pilot: yes)
The agent runs this same command, then applies the verb's card (sb help {0}).

sb.verb.open.does:
Measures where you are: in a project, its identity card, its repository and the workspace root;
in the Vault, the session preflight. Then your agent reads the state files in order
and gives the verdict on its first line.

sb.verb.install.does:
Runs the installation's last steps, in order, each one only if needed:
1. puts sb on your user PATH;
2. adds the Claude Code marketplace second-brain;
3. installs the plugin sb, so that /sb:<verb> exists;
4. declares the Vault's MCP server in every tool present — the Claude app, Claude Code, Codex,
   Gemini CLI, Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, LM Studio (the Pilot's access to your files);
   --mcp --label <label> gives it a shorter name.
--path, --plugin or --mcp runs one step alone; --run resumes or repairs the installation.
